{"item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/biketourhawaii/items/20498/", "pk": 20498, "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/biketourhawaii/", "pk": 6798, "shortname": "biketourhawaii", "name": "Bike Tour Hawaii", "processor_currency": "usd", "display_processor_currency": "US dollars"}, "name": "Diamond Head Bike to Hike", "is_retail": false, "is_archived": false, "is_private": false, "color": 3, "unicode": "Diamond Head Bike to Hike", "is_bookable_ever_by_phone": false, "sold_out_text": "", "cutoff_unreached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_unreached_hours": 6.0, "is_cutoff_unreached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_unreached_call_to_book_text": "", "cutoff_reached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_reached_hours": 0.0, "is_cutoff_reached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_reached_call_to_book_text": "", "minimum_initial_party_size": 1, "minimum_subsequent_party_size": 1, "maximum_initial_party_size": null, "maximum_subsequent_party_size": null, "auto_open_kind": "before-start", "auto_open_hours": null, "is_waitlist_when_full": false, "is_unlisted": false, "booking_restriction": null, "is_card_required": false, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": -2495, "description": "#Challenge yourself with adventure!\n\n##Duration\n3-4 Hours\n\n##About\nWe meet early at 7:00 am to avoid crowds and the heat on the crater trial.  After your bike fitting and safety instruction, we roll onto Kapiolani Park to discover its history then we head down to the WW1 Natatorium Memorial to see where famed Duke Kahanamoku and others trained for the Olympics.  You’ll get to visit a secluded green sand beach at the base of Diamond Head; see the Disney house and roll past other homes from the marvels of wealth. We then pedal up 150 feet to the Diamond Head Light House Lookout. From this advantageous view, you can see the surfers enjoying the placid waters of Paradise.\nWhile getting photos with the Amelia Earhart memorial, we'll observe Doris Duke’s Shangri-La museum located in the wealthy Black Point neighborhood. After a short 100' elevation gain, we arrive near the Hawaii FIVE-O / NCIS Hawaii studios where they film ongoing TV series.  Next, we head into Diamond Head Crater's 150' climb and park our bikes for a 45-minute to 1-hour hike, a 300' climb filled with lots of Hawaiian and WWI history.  Along the way, you’ll experience incredible views of Oahu’s south and east-facing shores.  After the hike and photos, we descend to a healthy local inclusive lunch.  Sunscreen, water, sports drinks, and snacks are provided.   \n\n**NOTE:  This tour has hilly terrain and includes a walking hike to the top of Diamond Head.  Bike Tour Ride and Hike total, 8 Miles.  (3.5– 4 hours)   Maximum guests 8** \n \nMeet at the Kuhio Beach Banyan Tree, Waikiki Beach.", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "Meet at the Kuhio Beach Banyan Tree, Waikiki Beach 8:15 am.  After your bike fitting and safety instruction, we roll onto Kapiolani Park to discover its history then we head down to the WW1 Natatorium Memorial to see where famed Duke Kahanamoku and others trained for the Olympics.  You’ll get to visit a secluded green sand beach at the base of Diamond Head; see the Disney house and roll past other homes from the marvels of wealth. We then pedal up 150 feet to the Diamond Head Light House Lookout. From this advantageous view, you can see the surfers enjoying the placid waters of Paradise.\nFrom here, we ride on to visit Doris Duke’s Shangri-La located in the wealthy Black Point neighborhood. After a short climb, we arrive at the Hawaii FIVE-O studios where they film this ongoing series.  Next, we head into Diamond Head Crater and park our bikes for a 45 minute to 1 hour hike filled with lots of Hawaiian and WWII history.  Along the way, you’ll experience incredible views of Oahu’s south and east facing shores.  After the hike and photos we head down to a healthy local lunch on us.  This is followed by a visit to Lawson’s Station in Waikiki for a sweet “Dole Whip” soft serve ice cream.  Sunscreen, water, sports drink and Hawaiian snacks provided.   **NOTE:  This tour has hilly terrain and includes a walking hike to the top of Diamond Head.  Recommended for more Advanced Riders/Adventure Seekers.  Tour Ride 9 – 12 Miles. (3 – 4 hours)", "location": "Honolulu Hawaii, Waikiki", "booking_notes": "NOTE: This tour has hilly terrain and includes a walking hike to the top of Diamond Head. Sunscreen, water, sports drink, and snacks are provided.", "cancellation_notes": "Full refund if canceled within 24 hours of the scheduled tour.", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "3-4 Hours • Activity seekers favorite • Mountain Terrain • Daily 7:00 am", "short_description": "", "image_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/jKjh8oV4RGKuUfB9jHGd", "image_cdn_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/jKjh8oV4RGKuUfB9jHGd", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/biketourhawaii/items/20498/images/32523/", "pk": 32523, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https://www.filepicker.io/api/file/4qCiAdGQQbOrqUBViZem", "image_cdn_url": "https://www.filepicker.io/api/file/4qCiAdGQQbOrqUBViZem", "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/biketourhawaii/"}, "item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/biketourhawaii/items/20498/"}, "crop": {"y": 0, "x": 0, "width": 1791, "url": "https://www.filepicker.io/api/file/NbBdP1xeS4W5IIMNA0u5", "height": 942}, "cropped_url": "https://www.filepicker.io/api/file/NbBdP1xeS4W5IIMNA0u5", "cropped_cdn_url": "https://www.filepicker.io/api/file/NbBdP1xeS4W5IIMNA0u5", "is_low_resolution": false, "has_text_overlay": true, "has_logo_overlay": false}, {"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/biketourhawaii/items/20498/images/399810/", "pk": 399810, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/y8ASo4gITNO2LB1